From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 13:06:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 84/85] web-app: fit the phone recording row on one line, show
 the meter again
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 0074 phone layout wrapped the recorder onto two rows and both were
mostly empty: row 1 held pause/mic/timer then a wide gap before the
picker, row 2 held ~200px of gap before Cancel/OK. The gap was the level
meter, which the `max-width: 400px` block hid while its container kept
`flex: 1` — so a phone recording showed no level feedback at all, and
the space it would have used sat empty one row below.

With the original-audio pill gone (previous patch) the only thing still
forcing the wrap is the fixed `width: 85px` on Cancel/OK, ~20px more
than either label needs. Dropping it leaves pause+mic+timer+meter+
picker+cancel+ok at roughly 353px of a 380px content box, so the row
fits on one line and the meter can come back — the `max-width: 400px`
block goes with it.

`flex-wrap: wrap` stays as a safety net for locales with longer labels.

Button height goes 32px -> 40px while the fixed width goes away. 32px is
under the 44px touch-target guidance, and a mis-tap on Cancel discards
the recording.
---
 .../AudioRecorder/styles.module.scss          | 26 +++++++------------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/styles.module.scss b/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/styles.module.scss
index f0e2739..560a6dc 100644
--- a/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/styles.module.scss
+++ b/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/styles.module.scss
@@ -158,22 +158,6 @@
   max-width: 56px;
 }
 
-// Below 400px the meter is hidden to make room for Timer/Cancel/OK; the live
-// waveform must hide too (its min-width would otherwise squeeze the buttons).
-// Hide only the inner bar/canvas, not the flex:1 container spacer.
-@media (max-width: 400px) {
-  .volumeBarContainer {
-    .volumeBar {
-      display: none;
-    }
-  }
-  // Compound selector: the base .liveWaveform rule is declared later in this
-  // file and would win a same-specificity tie, un-hiding the waveform.
-  .liveWaveformContainer .liveWaveform {
-    display: none;
-  }
-}
-
 // Live recorder waveform (experimental; replaces .volumeBarContainer when the
 // custom audio-player controls setting is on). Shares .volumeBar's footprint.
 .liveWaveformContainer {
@@ -356,8 +340,18 @@
   // (and `.audioRecorder .stopRecording.stopRecording`). Same specificity +
   // later source order → these win. Without the prefix the base out-ranked them
   // and the desktop margins leaked onto the phone layout.
+  //
+  // The base block's fixed `width: 85px` is ~20px wider than either label
+  // needs. Dropping it is what gets pause+mic+timer+meter+picker+cancel+ok
+  // onto one line at 390px, so the meter no longer has to be hidden to make
+  // room for the buttons. 40px height: 32px sits under the 44px touch-target
+  // guidance, and a mis-tap on Cancel discards the recording.
   .audioRecorder .cancel,
   .audioRecorder .stopRecording {
+    width: auto;
+    padding: 0 12px;
+    height: 40px;
+    margin-top: 0;
     margin-inline-start: 6px;
   }
   .audioRecorder .stopRecording.stopRecording {
